1
00:00:03,857 --> 00:00:06,500
The Lives of the Prophets, Part 1

2
00:00:06,746 --> 00:00:10,356
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:10,706 --> 00:00:14,722
They lost in the Battle of dialogue.

4
00:00:15,531 --> 00:00:20,510
They lost up till that moment it was a dialogue between Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and them.

5
00:00:22,383 --> 00:00:30,137
Whenever the Kuffar(كفار) lose in the battle of dialogue, they don't admit

6
00:00:31,502 --> 00:00:37,822
and they go to the next level and that is actual fighting and physical fighting.

7
00:00:38,496 --> 00:00:39,956
They did that with Muhammadﷺ

8
00:00:39,986 --> 00:00:42,044
Muhammadﷺ had a dialogue with them.

9
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:46,481
And they were arguing in the beginning and they obviously definitely lost,

10
00:00:46,735 --> 00:00:51,398
you cannot stand against the Hujjah(حجة) of Allah سبحانه تعالى the evidence of Qur'an you can't stand against it.

11
00:00:51,962 --> 00:00:56,779
So when they lost in the field of dialogue, then they resulted to force.

12
00:00:57,589 --> 00:00:58,441
قالوا حَرِّقوهُ

13
00:00:58,472 --> 00:00:58,953
Burn him.

14
00:00:58,977 --> 00:01:03,391
We can't deal with him, we can't debate with him with our minds, burn him.

15
00:01:04,177 --> 00:01:10,582
قالوا حَرِّقوهُ وَانصُروا آلِهَتَكُم إِن كُنتُم فاعِلينَ۝

16
00:01:10,642 --> 00:01:14,256
They said burn him and help your Gods, if you will be doing.

17
00:01:14,621 --> 00:01:15,525
Burn him.

18
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:19,153
This is an admission of failure.

19
00:01:19,732 --> 00:01:22,778
When they said: Burn him! This is an admission of failure.

20
00:01:22,810 --> 00:01:27,517
It's an admission from their side that they're not able to have a dialogue with him.

21
00:01:27,897 --> 00:01:31,276
They lost, they resulted to force.

22
00:01:32,816 --> 00:01:38,978
It says in the books of Tafseer(تفسير) that they set up a fire it took them days and days to gather the wood for it.

23
00:01:40,311 --> 00:01:44,294
And they set up this trench and they filled it with logs

24
00:01:45,222 --> 00:01:54,647
and they set fire to it and the flames are so high that a bird would fly over it and fall down dead, huge fire.

25
00:01:56,322 --> 00:01:59,897
And they had to throw Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) with a catapult, Manjneeq(منجنيق).

26
00:02:01,905 --> 00:02:11,184
So they put Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) in this catapult and they threw him, in the fire.

27
00:02:13,922 --> 00:02:16,182
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) landed in the fire.

28
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:21,198
Fire, which we know burns.

29
00:02:22,143 --> 00:02:23,811
But who's the One, Who created fire?

30
00:02:24,136 --> 00:02:25,279
Allah سبحانه وتعالى

31
00:02:25,597 --> 00:02:27,795
and Who is the One, Who made fire burn?

32
00:02:28,176 --> 00:02:29,557
Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

33
00:02:31,065 --> 00:02:35,241
Are the laws of nature mandatory on Allah سبحانه وتعالى Allah has to follow them.?

34
00:02:35,701 --> 00:02:38,408
Allah is the One, Who created these laws to start with.

35
00:02:39,463 --> 00:02:45,868
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى, who created the fire to burn, can make the fire and air condition.

36
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:49,822
Ibrahim عليه السّلام landed in this fire, that burns.

37
00:02:50,616 --> 00:02:54,557
Allah سبحانه وتعالى ordered the fire because the fire is a servant of Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

38
00:02:54,772 --> 00:03:00,526
قُلنا يا نارُ كوني بَردًا وَسَلامًا عَلىٰ إِبراهيمَ۝

39
00:03:00,684 --> 00:03:06,033
Oh fire! Be cool and peace, tranquility on Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

40
00:03:06,993 --> 00:03:09,902
It is said that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) later, would say

41
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:15,067
that the most pleasant moments that I had in my life were those moments when I was sitting in the fire.

42
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:19,998
The best moments that he had in his life the most peaceful moments,

43
00:03:20,546 --> 00:03:24,042
were those moments when Allah سبحانه وتعالى told the burning fire;

44
00:03:24,201 --> 00:03:27,280
قُلنا يا نارُ كوني بَردًا وَسَلامًا عَلىٰ إِبراهيمَ۝

45
00:03:27,471 --> 00:03:31,428
Oh fire! Be you coolness and safety for Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

46
00:03:32,904 --> 00:03:35,610
Allah سبحانه وتعالى can change everything for you.

47
00:03:36,222 --> 00:03:38,793
Allah made the sun stop, for Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون),

48
00:03:39,110 --> 00:03:42,184
Allah سبحانه وتعالى made the sea split for Musa(موسى),

49
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:47,354
Allah سبحانه وتعالى made all diseases vanish under the hand of Syedina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى),

50
00:03:47,525 --> 00:03:51,812
Allah سبحانه وتعالى made the moon split, for Muhammadﷺ,

51
00:03:52,518 --> 00:03:57,285
Allah سبحانه وتعالى made the fire wholeness and safety for Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

52
00:03:58,666 --> 00:04:03,765
Allah سبحانه وتعالى can do whatever He wants for the believer,

53
00:04:03,796 --> 00:04:08,795
we have to have trust in Allah سبحانه وتعالى and Tawakkul(توكل) that Allah will give you victory, if you follow the orders of Allah.

54
00:04:09,637 --> 00:04:11,954
You don't need anything else, you don't need anything.

55
00:04:12,684 --> 00:04:18,436
All what we need is Allah سبحانه وتعالى, all what you need is Allah سبحانه وتعالى,

56
00:04:18,571 --> 00:04:22,190
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), and what was the Dua(دُعَا) of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), when he was thrown in the fire?

57
00:04:23,983 --> 00:04:25,880
حسبي الله ونعم الوكيل

58
00:04:26,467 --> 00:04:33,396
Allah is sufficient for me, Allah is enough, I do not need the help of anyone.

59
00:04:33,486 --> 00:04:39,054
Allah is sufficient for me and He is the best Disposer of affairs.

60
00:04:40,165 --> 00:04:42,809
I do not need anyone but Allah سبحانه وتعالى,

61
00:04:43,254 --> 00:04:47,611
it says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ), Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) said;

62
00:04:48,412 --> 00:04:53,469
حَسْبُنَا اللَّهُ ونِعْمَ الوَكِيلُ، قالَهَا إبْرَاهِيمُ عليه السَّلَامُ حِينَ أُلْقِيَ في النَّارِ،

63
00:04:53,945 --> 00:04:56,585
وقالَهَا مُحَمَّدٌ صلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّم

64
00:04:56,834 --> 00:05:04,587
حِينَ قالوا: إِنَّ النَّاسَ قَدْ جَمَعُوا لَكُمْ فَاخْشَوْهُمْ فَزَادَهُمْ إِيمَانًا وَقَالُوا حَسْبُنَا اللَّهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيلُ

65
00:05:05,373 --> 00:05:06,405
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) says;

66
00:05:06,465 --> 00:05:08,231
حسبي الله ونعم الوكيل

67
00:05:08,374 --> 00:05:11,533
Allah is sufficient for us and the best disposal of our affairs.

68
00:05:11,874 --> 00:05:14,358
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said it, when he was thrown in the fire

69
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:20,643
and Muhammadﷺ said it, when he was threatened and told that the enemies are gathering for you so fear them

70
00:05:20,944 --> 00:05:23,690
 that made them increase in their Eeman(ايمان).

71
00:05:23,833 --> 00:05:27,182
And they said Allah sufficient for us and is the best Disposer of affairs.

72
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:35,606
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was threatened, that the enemies are mobilizing and gathering to fight you, so fear them

73
00:05:35,907 --> 00:05:38,709
the people were telling Muhammadﷺ to fear the enemy.

74
00:05:38,931 --> 00:05:39,821
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

75
00:05:39,851 --> 00:05:40,743
فَزَادَهُمْ إِيمَانًا

76
00:05:40,773 --> 00:05:42,434
that made their Eeman(ايمان) increase.

77
00:05:44,172 --> 00:05:45,519
Allah سبحانه تعالى says;

78
00:05:45,685 --> 00:05:50,584
وَأَرادوا بِهِ كَيدًا فَجَعَلناهُمُ الأَخسَرينَ۝

79
00:05:50,614 --> 00:05:53,517
And they wanted to harm him, but we made them the worst losers,

80
00:05:54,088 --> 00:06:01,443
وَنَجَّيناهُ وَلوطًا إِلَى الأَرضِ الَّتي بارَكنا فيها لِلعالَمينَ۝

81
00:06:01,522 --> 00:06:06,030
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says: And we saved him and Lut(لوط) to the land which we blessed,

82
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:09,823
and we'll get to that in the Hijrah(هجرة) of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), later.

83
00:06:10,172 --> 00:06:16,260
After this event happened, the king of Babylon at the time was An-Namrood(ألنمرود).

84
00:06:17,014 --> 00:06:19,903
So An-Namrood(ألنمرود) heard about this young man, who performed this miracle.

85
00:06:20,490 --> 00:06:21,335
Who is he?

86
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,668
Bring him forward.

87
00:06:24,971 --> 00:06:29,665
So they brought Ibrahim عليه السّلام, this young man to debate with the king,

88
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:34,514
An-Namrood(ألنمرود), the powerful dictator tyrant, An-Namrood(ألنمرود).

89
00:06:36,609 --> 00:06:42,740
So, An-Namrood(ألنمرود) have this debate or dialogue with Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

90
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:50,649
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) told the king, Allah سبحانه وتعالى is the One, Who gives life and the One, Who takes it away.

91
00:06:51,237 --> 00:06:52,490
Can you do that?

92
00:06:54,905 --> 00:06:56,596
And An-Namrood(ألنمرود) said: Yes.

93
00:06:57,381 --> 00:06:59,542
I can give life and I can take it away.

94
00:07:01,494 --> 00:07:02,280
How?

95
00:07:02,518 --> 00:07:05,677
He said: Call two people from jail, call two men from jail.

96
00:07:05,899 --> 00:07:07,622
So they brought these two men from jail.

97
00:07:08,987 --> 00:07:11,733
He commanded his soldiers to execute one of them.

98
00:07:12,295 --> 00:07:13,911
And he told the second one, you're free.

99
00:07:14,816 --> 00:07:21,944
He said: See, I took away the life of this one, and I gave the life to the other one.

100
00:07:23,341 --> 00:07:28,595
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) didn't mean this foolish, shallow meaning of giving life and death.

101
00:07:29,206 --> 00:07:34,478
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was talking about the miracle of life which is occurring in every single moment of the day and night.

102
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:41,124
Where Allah سبحانه وتعالى is giving life in every single moment of the day and night to a new creature.

103
00:07:41,513 --> 00:07:43,870
That is the meaning that Ibrahim عليه السّلام meant.

104
00:07:44,291 --> 00:07:52,321
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) is not going to go and argue with the king in this point and this is a pointer in debate.

105
00:07:53,083 --> 00:08:04,863
If you find that the opponent is trying to trap you with an insignificant point or discussion, leave it.

106
00:08:05,053 --> 00:08:07,736
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) did not respond to this,

107
00:08:08,157 --> 00:08:10,284
 Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) completely changed the subject.

108
00:08:10,577 --> 00:08:12,872
And since he saw that this man is stubborn,

109
00:08:13,086 --> 00:08:19,304
and he is going to debate and dialogue with this way, and argue in this fashion, I'm going to get him from another angle.

110
00:08:19,915 --> 00:08:23,762
To close the discussion with him, I'm not going to go down that road with him.

111
00:08:24,461 --> 00:08:29,603
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) completely left the issue of life and death alone, even though there's a lot that could be said in it.

112
00:08:29,699 --> 00:08:32,804
But Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) did not debate that point, fine.

113
00:08:33,158 --> 00:08:34,040
He chose another point.

114
00:08:34,134 --> 00:08:35,007
He said;

115
00:08:35,730 --> 00:08:39,275
Allah سبحانه وتعالى brings the sun from the east, bring it from the west.

116
00:08:39,736 --> 00:08:41,069
فَبُهِتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ

117
00:08:41,744 --> 00:08:47,074
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says; So the disbeliever was utterly defeated, he couldn't speak.

118
00:08:47,725 --> 00:08:50,106
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) shut him up with this argument.

119
00:08:51,297 --> 00:08:52,970
As I said, this is a pointer to the discussion

120
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,721
because you could have discussed the point of life and death with them and told him;

121
00:08:56,751 --> 00:08:59,083
No, this is not what I meant, what I meant is this and that.

122
00:08:59,298 --> 00:09:01,433
And it would be an endless fruitless discussion.

123
00:09:01,909 --> 00:09:08,028
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) chose another angle and through an evidence on him that cannot be rebutted.

124
00:09:09,013 --> 00:09:11,557
And he shut him up, that's it.

125
00:09:11,723 --> 00:09:14,795
فَبُهِتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ وَاللَّهُ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

126
00:09:14,969 --> 00:09:17,747
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى guides not the people, who are wrongdoers.

127
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,300
I'll read the Ayah(آية) to you.

128
00:09:19,570 --> 00:09:30,528
أَلَم تَرَ إِلَى الَّذي حاجَّ إِبراهيمَ في رَبِّهِ أَن آتاهُ اللَّهُ المُلكَ

129
00:09:30,948 --> 00:09:37,362
إِذ قالَ إِبراهيمُ رَبِّيَ الَّذي يُحيي وَيُميتُ

130
00:09:37,608 --> 00:09:41,187
قالَ أَنا أُحيي وَأُميتُ ۖ

131
00:09:41,465 --> 00:09:51,781
قالَ إِبراهيمُ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأتي بِالشَّمسِ مِنَ المَشرِقِ فَأتِ بِها مِنَ المَغرِبِ

132
00:09:52,252 --> 00:10:01,036
فَبُهِتَ الَّذي كَفَرَ ۗ وَاللَّهُ لا يَهدِي القَومَ الظّالِمينَ۝

133
00:10:01,066 --> 00:10:07,242
Have you not thought about him, who disputed with Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) about his Lord, Allah.

134
00:10:07,528 --> 00:10:09,413
Because Allah has given him the kingdom.

135
00:10:09,946 --> 00:10:15,470
When Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said to him, My lord is He, Who gives life and causes death,

136
00:10:15,803 --> 00:10:18,304
he said, I give life and cause death.

137
00:10:18,781 --> 00:10:25,138
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said: Verily Allah causes the sun to rise from the east, then causes you to rise from the west.

138
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:32,607
So the disbeliever was utterly defeated and Allah guides not the people who are Dhalimeen(ظالمين), the wrongdoers.

139
00:10:33,663 --> 00:10:37,205
We can see in this discussion that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) has a strong level of Yaqeen(يقين),

140
00:10:37,681 --> 00:10:42,380
a strong level of conviction, certainty, in Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

141
00:10:44,410 --> 00:10:51,363
In the issue of life and death, Ibrahim عليه السّلام had Ilm Al-Yaqeen(علم اليقين), certain knowledge.

142
00:10:52,005 --> 00:10:57,732
His knowledge was certain, they cannot shake the man of Ibrahim عليه السّلام in this point.

143
00:10:59,064 --> 00:11:03,136
He knew that Allah is the one who gives life and he knew that Allah was the One, Who takes it away.

144
00:11:04,564 --> 00:11:08,617
But Ibrahim عليه السّلام wants to reach through the level of Ain Ul-Yaqeen(عين اليقين).

145
00:11:10,522 --> 00:11:16,249
Ain Ul-Yaqeen(عين اليقين) is certainty by seeing or witnessing.

146
00:11:18,214 --> 00:11:22,484
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) had Ilm Al-Yaqeen(علم اليقين), the knowledge of Yaqeen(يقين), the certain knowledge,

147
00:11:22,888 --> 00:11:30,081
but he wants to reach to the level of certain certainty with witnessing or seeing.

148
00:11:31,383 --> 00:11:34,656
So Ibrahim عليه السّلام has no doubts in Allah سبحانه وتعالى

149
00:11:34,686 --> 00:11:37,950
because this argument that he made with the king is based on certain knowledge

150
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:43,323
you can't argue like that about life and death when your knowledge is shakable or Eeman(ايمان) is shakable.

151
00:11:43,934 --> 00:11:47,514
Sometimes we read the Ayah(آية), the Ayah(آية) that I'm gonna read right now.

152
00:11:47,649 --> 00:11:49,715
And we think that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) had doubts in Allah.

153
00:11:49,745 --> 00:11:50,525
No! He didn't.

154
00:11:50,843 --> 00:11:53,319
He had Ilm Al-Yaqeen(علم اليقين), certain knowledge,

155
00:11:53,605 --> 00:11:56,812
but he just wants to reach to the level of Ain Ul-Yaqeen(عين اليقين).

156
00:11:57,335 --> 00:11:58,304
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

157
00:11:58,364 --> 00:12:05,275
وَإِذ قالَ إِبراهيمُ رَبِّ أَرِني كَيفَ تُحيِي المَوتىٰ ۖ

158
00:12:05,305 --> 00:12:06,607
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

159
00:12:06,869 --> 00:12:11,265
And remember when Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said: My Lord, show me how you give life to the dead?

160
00:12:12,353 --> 00:12:13,972
Show me, he wants to see it.

161
00:12:14,353 --> 00:12:17,130
That does not mean that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) does not believe in it.

162
00:12:17,249 --> 00:12:18,400
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) does believe in it.

163
00:12:18,701 --> 00:12:22,511
And his argument with the king was based on that belief, but he wants to see it.

164
00:12:22,884 --> 00:12:23,663
So Allah asked him;

165
00:12:23,693 --> 00:12:24,917
قالَ أَوَلَم تُؤمِن ۖ

166
00:12:25,274 --> 00:12:27,959
Allah said: Do you not believe.

167
00:12:28,061 --> 00:12:29,029
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said;

168
00:12:29,307 --> 00:12:34,886
قالَ بَلىٰ وَلٰكِن لِيَطمَئِنَّ قَلبي ۖ

169
00:12:34,950 --> 00:12:38,161
He said: Yes! I believe, but to be stronger faith.

170
00:12:38,585 --> 00:12:41,242
I do believe, but I want to be stronger faith.

171
00:12:42,695 --> 00:12:46,655
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى told Ibrahim عليه السّلام take birds, four birds.

172
00:12:48,804 --> 00:12:56,580
slaughter them, chop them into pieces, grind them, not ground beeds, ground birds.

173
00:12:57,707 --> 00:12:58,707
Grind them together.

174
00:12:59,175 --> 00:13:06,694
Mix these four Birds together, mesh the flesh, so it's inseparable.

175
00:13:07,234 --> 00:13:14,849
And then split this mixture into four parts and put one part on the top of a mountain.

176
00:13:14,912 --> 00:13:23,201
So you have four mountains, a quarter of this ground birds, put the quarter of it on a top of a mountain

177
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:25,415
and then call them.

178
00:13:26,911 --> 00:13:32,826
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) put these four quarters of ground bird on the tops of these four mountains.

179
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:35,771
And then he called them, he said: Come.

180
00:13:37,183 --> 00:13:43,355
All of these birds came together alive, four birds.

181
00:13:44,244 --> 00:13:48,773
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) witnessed the miracle of life in front of his eyes.

182
00:13:49,609 --> 00:13:51,156
Allah سبحانه تعالى says;

183
00:13:51,553 --> 00:13:58,643
وَإِذ قالَ إِبراهيمُ رَبِّ أَرِني كَيفَ تُحيِي المَوتىٰ ۖ

184
00:13:58,881 --> 00:14:01,492
قالَ أَوَلَم تُؤمِن ۖ

185
00:14:01,675 --> 00:14:07,338
قالَ بَلىٰ وَلٰكِن لِيَطمَئِنَّ قَلبي ۖ

186
00:14:07,545 --> 00:14:12,640
قالَ فَخُذ أَربَعَةً مِنَ الطَّيرِ

187
00:14:12,915 --> 00:14:16,272
فَصُرهُنَّ إِلَيكَ

188
00:14:16,415 --> 00:14:23,254
ثُمَّ اجعَل عَلىٰ كُلِّ جَبَلٍ مِنهُنَّ جُزءًا

189
00:14:23,468 --> 00:14:28,703
 ثُمَّ ادعُهُنَّ يَأتينَكَ سَعيًا ۚ

190
00:14:28,862 --> 00:14:35,210
وَاعلَم أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَزيزٌ حَكيمٌ۝

191
00:14:35,457 --> 00:14:36,920
And remember what Abraham said;

192
00:14:37,087 --> 00:14:39,396
My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead.

193
00:14:39,698 --> 00:14:41,849
He (Allah) said, Do you not believe?

194
00:14:41,928 --> 00:14:44,881
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said: Yes! I believe but to be stronger in faith,

195
00:14:44,976 --> 00:14:49,777
Allah said: Take four birds then cause them to incline towards you.

196
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:56,929
And then put a portion of them on every hill and call them they will come to you in haste

197
00:14:57,342 --> 00:15:01,032
and know that Allah is Almighty, all Wise.

198
00:15:03,477 --> 00:15:05,906
Ibrahim عليه السّلام made Da'wah(دعوة) to his people.

199
00:15:06,263 --> 00:15:15,632
And after all of his efforts and the miracle of Ibrahim عليه السّلام being saved from the fire.

200
00:15:16,569 --> 00:15:22,429
Nobody believed in Ibrahim عليه السّلام except his nephew.

201
00:15:23,588 --> 00:15:25,088
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

202
00:15:25,148 --> 00:15:28,095
فَـَٔامَنَ لَهُۥ لُوطٌ ۘ

203
00:15:28,436 --> 00:15:30,134
Lut(لوط) believed in Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

204
00:15:30,976 --> 00:15:34,381
Lut(لوط) is the nephew of Sayyedina Ibrahim عليه السّلام,

205
00:15:34,984 --> 00:15:40,176
after all of this effort, after this miracle happening in front of the eyes of this nation,

206
00:15:40,579 --> 00:15:44,113
nobody believed in him except his nephew, Lut عليه السّلام.

207
00:15:44,891 --> 00:15:46,097
And they had to leave.

208
00:15:46,970 --> 00:15:50,659
They had to flee from the persecution and the oppression of their homeland.

209
00:15:51,262 --> 00:15:58,697
They had to give up the land of their birth and the land where they were raised up and go and find another land to worship Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

210
00:15:58,911 --> 00:16:00,451
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

211
00:16:00,776 --> 00:16:05,856
وَقالَ إِنّي مُهاجِرٌ إِلىٰ رَبّي ۖ

212
00:16:06,157 --> 00:16:10,616
إِنَّهُ هُوَ العَزيزُ الحَكيم۝

213
00:16:10,862 --> 00:16:14,417
I will immigrate for the sake of my Lord.

214
00:16:14,790 --> 00:16:17,355
Verily he is the Almighty the all Wise.

215
00:16:18,625 --> 00:16:20,640
Where was Ibrahim عليه السّلام heading.?

216
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:22,672
Allah سبحانه تعالى says;

217
00:16:22,950 --> 00:16:31,638
وَنَجَّيْنَٰهُ وَلُوطًا إِلَى ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلَّتِى بَٰرَكْنَا فِيهَا لِلْعَٰلَمِينَ۝

218
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:32,832
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

219
00:16:32,862 --> 00:16:40,657
And we rescued him and Lut(لوط) in english LOT, to the land which we have blessed for the mankind for the world.

220
00:16:41,411 --> 00:16:49,490
And the blessed land is the Holy Land Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) which is composed today of four countries

221
00:16:50,069 --> 00:16:55,791
because everything in the Muslim world has split up, in the past, that was Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

222
00:16:57,037 --> 00:17:01,426
Now it is Syria, Falastine(فلسطين), Lebanon and Jordan.

223
00:17:02,466 --> 00:17:07,595
And the center of it all and the holiest of it, is Jerusalem Bait-Ul-Maqsad(بيت المقدس).

224
00:17:09,484 --> 00:17:14,051
This is their direction, Sayidina Ibrahim عليه السّلام was heading for.

225
00:17:14,964 --> 00:17:19,567
On the way he passed through a land called Harran(حرَّان) in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

226
00:17:21,289 --> 00:17:24,825
And the people of Harran(حرَّان) used to worship, the stars.

227
00:17:26,476 --> 00:17:28,746
They had a very pretty flexible religion.

228
00:17:29,492 --> 00:17:31,659
They would go out at night at nighttime,

229
00:17:32,032 --> 00:17:36,543
and they would look at the sky and everyone will make a choice and pick a star and they would worship

230
00:17:37,155 --> 00:17:38,393
that was their Ibadah(عبادة)

231
00:17:39,194 --> 00:17:42,676
somebody would worship Venus, someone other would worship another star.

232
00:17:43,049 --> 00:17:53,204
That's how their religion was, it's not very different of what we think of as modern religions today.

233
00:17:56,029 --> 00:18:00,990
Ibrahim عليه السّلام had his own way of Da'wah(دعوة).

234
00:18:02,403 --> 00:18:06,181
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) had his style of Da'wah(دعوة).

235
00:18:06,824 --> 00:18:11,420
You remember how he made his Da'wah(دعوة), to his people?

236
00:18:11,777 --> 00:18:17,269
He went and destroyed all of the idols and then he hang the axe on the biggest idol.

237
00:18:18,793 --> 00:18:22,648
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) over here, how is he making Da'wah(دعوة) to these people?

238
00:18:23,349 --> 00:18:24,936
He went out with them at night.

239
00:18:25,857 --> 00:18:27,658
They went out to worship.

240
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:33,341
The first star that comes up is not the star it's a planet.

241
00:18:34,087 --> 00:18:40,816
And that is Venus, it is the first star that shines in the sky after sunset.

242
00:18:42,165 --> 00:18:45,197
It looks like a star but it's not it's Venus, the planet Venus.

243
00:18:45,727 --> 00:18:49,038
Ibrahim عليه السّلام said: This is my God.

244
00:18:49,443 --> 00:18:55,795
فَلَمّا جَنَّ عَلَيهِ اللَّيلُ رَأىٰ كَوكَبًا ۖ قالَ هٰذا رَبّي ۖ

245
00:18:55,825 --> 00:18:59,803
When the knight covered him over with darkness he saw star he said this is my Lord,

246
00:18:59,946 --> 00:19:07,237
in front of everyone he said, This is my Lord and then the planet set, he said;

247
00:19:07,267 --> 00:19:12,233
فَلَمّا أَفَلَ قالَ لا أُحِبُّ الآفِلينَ۝

248
00:19:12,263 --> 00:19:14,781
I do not like those that set.

249
00:19:15,392 --> 00:19:17,825
This cannot be my God because it sets.

250
00:19:20,777 --> 00:19:22,940
And then he saw the moon.

251
00:19:23,242 --> 00:19:26,234
The next day he said: The moon is my Lord.

252
00:19:26,432 --> 00:19:31,547
فَلَمّا رَأَى القَمَرَ بازِغًا قالَ هٰذا رَبّي ۖ

253
00:19:31,577 --> 00:19:33,643
He saw the moon, he said this is my Lord

254
00:19:34,254 --> 00:19:35,397
and then the moon set.

255
00:19:35,659 --> 00:19:36,166
So he said;

256
00:19:36,226 --> 00:19:45,926
فَلَمّا أَفَلَ قالَ لَئِن لَم يَهدِني رَبّي لَأَكونَنَّ مِنَ القَومِ الضّالّينَ۝

257
00:19:45,956 --> 00:19:50,409
Unless my Lord guides me, I shall surely be among the err on people.

258
00:19:51,115 --> 00:19:54,979
So he said: In front of everyone, if Allah does not guide me, I'm gonna be one of those who are misguided.

259
00:19:56,375 --> 00:19:58,058
And then the sun came up,

260
00:19:58,296 --> 00:20:05,028
فَلَمّا رَأَى الشَّمسَ بازِغَةً قالَ هٰذا رَبّي هٰذا أَكبَرُ ۖ

261
00:20:05,088 --> 00:20:07,012
This is my lord it's the biggest.

262
00:20:07,821 --> 00:20:11,605
 And he pretended that he's worshipping the sun, and then the sun set.

263
00:20:11,922 --> 00:20:14,414
And then finally, Syedina Ibrahim(سيدنا اِبْراهِيْم) said;

264
00:20:14,533 --> 00:20:23,025
فَلَمّا أَفَلَت قالَ يا قَومِ إِنّي بَريءٌ مِمّا تُشرِكونَ۝

265
00:20:23,399 --> 00:20:32,241
إِنّي وَجَّهتُ وَجهِيَ لِلَّذي فَطَرَ السَّماواتِ وَالأَرضَ حَنيفًا ۖ وَما أَنا مِنَ المُشرِكينَ۝

266
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:36,917
I'm indeed free from all that you join as partners in worship with Allah.

267
00:20:37,171 --> 00:20:42,913
Verily, I have turned my face towards Him, Who has created the heavens on Earth, Haneefah(حنيفة).

268
00:20:43,227 --> 00:20:45,545
Haneefah(حنيفة) is on the straight path.

269
00:20:45,838 --> 00:20:49,783
And I am not of those who are Mushrikeen(مشركين), the ones, who associate other gods with Allah.

270
00:20:50,235 --> 00:20:53,855
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) is doing this presentation in front of everyone.

271
00:20:53,885 --> 00:21:05,485
Now there are some Mufassireen(مفسرين) who tend to think that in these Ayaat(آيات) Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was searching for the truth.

272
00:21:07,284 --> 00:21:13,709
So they give the explanation that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) did not know the truth, and he was searching for the truth.

273
00:21:14,458 --> 00:21:17,421
And in the end, his search for the truth, led him to worship Allah.

274
00:21:17,451 --> 00:21:23,006
So in the beginning Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) started worshiping Venus and then he worshipped the moon and then he worshipped the sun.

275
00:21:23,272 --> 00:21:26,684
Finally, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) knew the truth and he worshiped Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

276
00:21:28,018 --> 00:21:33,751
But Al-Mufassir(ألمفسر) Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) strongly disagrees with this.

277
00:21:34,910 --> 00:21:36,400
He says this cannot be true.

278
00:21:37,354 --> 00:21:46,466
He said: We cannot expect from a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى to be misguided to worship the sun and the moon and planets.

279
00:21:48,442 --> 00:21:56,059
He said: If Allah سبحانه وتعالى has created the human being on Fitrah(فطرة) of Islam, if that's the original creation,

280
00:21:56,750 --> 00:22:04,449
how could a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah be misguided so bad that he would worship these stars and planets and not know the truth.

281
00:22:07,131 --> 00:22:15,131
And he mentioned some other evidences to refute this claim that this is a story of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) searching for the truth.

282
00:22:15,344 --> 00:22:16,124
He says: No.

283
00:22:16,275 --> 00:22:19,989
This was a Da'wah(دعوة) presentation that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was giving to the people.

284
00:22:21,045 --> 00:22:25,718
And he said: This comes after the Da'wah(دعوة) of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) to his own homeland.

285
00:22:26,845 --> 00:22:31,082
This comes after, because after Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) left, then he went to Harran(حرَّان)

286
00:22:31,298 --> 00:22:34,913
and in Harran(حرَّان), the people used to worship the planets, not in the homeland of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

287
00:22:34,943 --> 00:22:37,554
 in the homeland of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), they used to worship the idols.

288
00:22:38,633 --> 00:22:46,528
So after he moved out of Iraq, and he got to Harran(حرَّان), he saw the people worshipping these planets,

289
00:22:46,768 --> 00:22:48,870
then he started giving them this presentation.

290
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:51,651
Also Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says that

291
00:22:51,711 --> 00:22:56,928
the Ayah(آية) that comes before these Ayaat(آيات) that I recited to you,

292
00:22:57,389 --> 00:23:04,237
clearly shows that Ibrahim عليه السّلام was already given the guidance by Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

293
00:23:04,634 --> 00:23:06,391
And this Ayah(آية) is Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

294
00:23:06,463 --> 00:23:14,770
وَكَذٰلِكَ نُري إِبراهيمَ مَلَكوتَ السَّماواتِ وَالأَرضِ وَلِيَكونَ مِنَ الموقِنينَ۝

295
00:23:14,857 --> 00:23:19,933
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says, thus did we show Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) the kingdom of the heavens and the earth,

296
00:23:20,179 --> 00:23:23,901
that he may be of those who have faith with certainty.

297
00:23:25,417 --> 00:23:31,038
This Ayah(آية) is before the Ayaat(آيات) that we are talking about worshipping the sun, and the moon, and the stars.

298
00:23:31,650 --> 00:23:37,606
In this Ayah(آية) Allah سبحانه وتعالى is saying that we have shown Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), the kingdom of the heavens and the earth,

299
00:23:37,828 --> 00:23:42,312
so that he can be of those, who have faith with certainty.

300
00:23:43,947 --> 00:23:54,421
Meaning that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has disclosed to Sayidina Ibrahim عليه السّلام some Ilm(علم), some knowledge of the heavens and the earth,

301
00:23:54,826 --> 00:23:56,381
that other people don't have,

302
00:23:56,635 --> 00:24:04,469
and this special knowledge that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has disclose to Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) would elevate him to the level of Moqin(موقن), certain faith.

303
00:24:05,445 --> 00:24:07,957
How can we then say that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was searching for the truth?

304
00:24:08,672 --> 00:24:15,554
The word Muhajah(محاجة) or Hajahoo(حاجه) means they debated with him.

305
00:24:16,784 --> 00:24:22,586
We find that this word was not used with any other prophet more than Ibrahim عليه السّلام in Qur'an.

306
00:24:23,570 --> 00:24:30,203
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was continuously in debates and dialogues with others about Islam.

307
00:24:32,076 --> 00:24:35,451
He made a debate and a dialogue with the king.

308
00:24:36,038 --> 00:24:37,768
He made the dialogue with his people.

309
00:24:37,975 --> 00:24:42,713
And over here, he's making this debate and dialogue with the people of Harran(حرَّان).

310
00:24:42,983 --> 00:24:44,315
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

311
00:24:44,394 --> 00:24:48,346
وَحاجَّهُ قَومُهُ ۚ

312
00:24:48,664 --> 00:24:58,068
قالَ أَتُحاجّونّي فِي اللَّهِ وَقَد هَدانِ ۚ

313
00:24:59,091 --> 00:25:05,976
وَلا أَخافُ ما تُشرِكونَ بِهِ إِلّا أَن يَشاءَ رَبّي شَيئًا ۗ

314
00:25:06,381 --> 00:25:12,198
وَسِعَ رَبّي كُلَّ شَيءٍ عِلمًا ۗ أَفَلا تَتَذَكَّرونَ۝

315
00:25:12,579 --> 00:25:23,201
وَكَيفَ أَخافُ ما أَشرَكتُم وَلا تَخافونَ أَنَّكُم أَشرَكتُم بِاللَّهِ ما لَم يُنَزِّل بِهِ عَلَيكُم سُلطانًا ۚ

316
00:25:23,812 --> 00:25:30,463
فَأَيُّ الفَريقَينِ أَحَقُّ بِالأَمنِ ۖ إِن كُنتُم تَعلَمونَ۝

317
00:25:30,542 --> 00:25:37,859
Wahaajahoo Qaumo(وحاجه قومه), or it could be in general, because Qaumuhoo(قومه) could be referring to his people.

318
00:25:38,423 --> 00:25:42,391
But Ayah(آية) says: His people disputed with him.

319
00:25:42,883 --> 00:25:47,557
He said, Do you dispute with me concerning Allah, while He has guided me,

320
00:25:47,986 --> 00:25:52,422
and I have no fear from those, whom you associate with align worship.

321
00:25:53,121 --> 00:25:55,167
I fear nobody except Allah.

322
00:25:55,397 --> 00:25:59,199
My Lord comprehends in His knowledge, all things, Will you not then remember.

323
00:26:00,088 --> 00:26:03,959
And how should I fear those, whom you associate in worship with Allah,

324
00:26:04,232 --> 00:26:11,487
while you fear not that you have joined in worship with Allah, things for which He has not sent down to you any authority?

325
00:26:12,470 --> 00:26:16,528
So which of the two parties has more right to be in security?

326
00:26:16,758 --> 00:26:17,988
If you but know.

327
00:26:19,139 --> 00:26:22,959
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) is saying: Why should I fear your gods?

328
00:26:23,863 --> 00:26:25,356
When I have Allah with me?

329
00:26:27,086 --> 00:26:28,770
You are the ones, who should be afraid.

330
00:26:30,628 --> 00:26:35,296
This could seem to be a regular statement.

331
00:26:36,050 --> 00:26:37,557
What's the big deal about it?

332
00:26:38,772 --> 00:26:40,851
But think about it in the right context.

333
00:26:41,629 --> 00:26:50,471
Ibrahim عليه السّلام was one and he's facing the whole and he's telling them I'm not afraid of you.

334
00:26:51,051 --> 00:26:53,067
And I'm not afraid of your threats.

335
00:26:53,463 --> 00:26:55,338
And I have no fear of your gods.

336
00:26:55,838 --> 00:26:57,600
Because Allah سبحانه وتعالى is with me.

337
00:26:59,711 --> 00:27:02,966
Imagine, you standing alone against the nation.

338
00:27:05,022 --> 00:27:06,117
It's not simple.

339
00:27:06,863 --> 00:27:09,371
Facing the whole society telling them I'm not afraid of anything.

340
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:13,061
I have no fear of your Gods no fear of your threats, do whatever you want.

341
00:27:14,164 --> 00:27:18,977
And then he is not only telling them I don't have any fear, He is telling them I feel very, very secure.

342
00:27:20,119 --> 00:27:22,342
And you should feel insecure.

343
00:27:22,850 --> 00:27:27,328
Because Allah سبحانه وتعالى is on my side, and you have no one to help you and support you.

344
00:27:28,280 --> 00:27:31,336
And then Allah سبحانه وتعالى confirms what Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) has said.

345
00:27:31,503 --> 00:27:32,820
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

346
00:27:32,947 --> 00:27:43,392
الَّذينَ آمَنوا وَلَم يَلبِسوا إيمانَهُم بِظُلمٍ أُولٰئِكَ لَهُمُ الأَمنُ وَهُم مُهتَدونَ۝

347
00:27:43,422 --> 00:27:44,673
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

348
00:27:44,855 --> 00:27:50,800
It is those, who believe and confuse not their belief with any wrongdoing.

349
00:27:51,609 --> 00:27:54,403
For them only there is security.

350
00:27:55,224 --> 00:27:59,643
Only for them is their security and Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

351
00:27:59,673 --> 00:28:01,183
 and they are a guide.

352
00:28:02,215 --> 00:28:06,405
Allah سبحانه وتعالى will provide peace and security for the believers.

353
00:28:06,667 --> 00:28:08,124
وأنزل سكينته

354
00:28:08,544 --> 00:28:14,026
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has revealed His Sakinah(سكينة), the tranquility on the believers in some of the most critical moments,

355
00:28:14,056 --> 00:28:21,799
in Badr(بدر) and other difficult situations Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given the Momineen(مؤمنين) peace and security and tranquility.

356
00:28:23,370 --> 00:28:31,673
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى is telling us that Allah is the One, Who has given Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) that Hujjah(حجة), that ability to debate.

357
00:28:32,197 --> 00:28:37,576
وَتِلكَ حُجَّتُنا آتَيناها إِبراهيمَ عَلىٰ قَومِهِ ۚ

358
00:28:37,757 --> 00:28:45,925
نَرفَعُ دَرَجاتٍ مَن نَشاءُ ۗ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ حَكيمٌ عَليمٌ۝

359
00:28:45,985 --> 00:28:49,575
And that was our proof, which we gave Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) against his people

360
00:28:49,757 --> 00:28:54,721
we raise whom we will in degrees, certainly your Lord is all Wise all Knowing.

361
00:28:56,491 --> 00:28:58,911
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) now made his Hijrah(هجرة) out of Harran(حرَّان).

362
00:28:59,094 --> 00:29:01,576
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Ibrahim عليه السّلامlived the life of Hijrah(هجرة).

363
00:29:02,306 --> 00:29:04,941
So he left Harran(حرَّان) and he went to Egypt.

364
00:29:07,552 --> 00:29:13,998
When he got to Egypt, the news was carried to the king of Egypt at the time,

365
00:29:14,585 --> 00:29:19,817
that there is a man who is accompanying the most beautiful woman.

366
00:29:20,753 --> 00:29:22,999
They were referring to Sara رضي الله عنها.

367
00:29:24,753 --> 00:29:26,357
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

368
00:29:27,884 --> 00:29:34,448
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) never lied, except three times.

369
00:29:36,162 --> 00:29:39,123
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) never lied except three times.

370
00:29:41,774 --> 00:29:45,337
And you'll see that these three lies, don't even count as lies.

371
00:29:48,274 --> 00:29:53,137
Two of them are for the sake of Allah and I'm narrating to you the Hadith(حديث).

372
00:29:53,407 --> 00:29:54,296
Two of them,

373
00:29:54,693 --> 00:29:56,009
إثناني منها في ذات الله

374
00:29:56,069 --> 00:29:57,628
Two of them are in the sake of Allah.

375
00:29:58,859 --> 00:29:59,438
When he said;

376
00:29:59,468 --> 00:30:00,454
 إني ثقيم

377
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:01,925
and when he said;

378
00:30:02,036 --> 00:30:03,647
بل فعلهم كبيرهم هذا

379
00:30:04,925 --> 00:30:11,245
when Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said: I am ill, I am sick and when he said, the big one, is the one who did it.

380
00:30:12,317 --> 00:30:16,210
You remember when we talked about the people of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) that they would go out

381
00:30:16,313 --> 00:30:22,466
they had this special night in which they would, they would leave, their town and go out and celebrate.

382
00:30:22,783 --> 00:30:29,513
All the town they would leave, they would vacate the whole town, they would all go out and celebrate.

383
00:30:30,907 --> 00:30:32,835
So they wanted Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) to come with them.

384
00:30:33,193 --> 00:30:37,129
But Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) had the plan, he wanted to stay behind because he had the plan in mind.

385
00:30:38,804 --> 00:30:42,784
But he can't stay behind except if he has an excuse.

386
00:30:43,427 --> 00:30:45,800
So they told them: Why aren't you coming with us?

387
00:30:45,860 --> 00:30:47,094
He said: I'm sick.

388
00:30:48,887 --> 00:30:51,467
What they understood is that he's physically ill.

389
00:30:52,189 --> 00:30:57,159
What Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) meant inside is that he is sick of what they're doing.

390
00:30:59,627 --> 00:31:06,733
So that's a lie because he meant something other than what they understood.

391
00:31:08,223 --> 00:31:10,475
The second lie is

392
00:31:10,505 --> 00:31:16,805
when Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) destroyed all of the idols, he hang the axe on the big idol.

393
00:31:17,557 --> 00:31:20,970
And then when they came back and said: Who is the one, who destroyed the idols?

394
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,451
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said: He did.

395
00:31:24,402 --> 00:31:26,733
Now, obviously, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) knows that he's not the one, who did it.

396
00:31:27,289 --> 00:31:29,559
But Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) wants to drive a point home.

397
00:31:29,589 --> 00:31:35,610
He wants to tell them go and talk to your Gods go and seek help from them.

398
00:31:35,792 --> 00:31:37,141
If they can do you any help.

399
00:31:38,729 --> 00:31:40,938
So these are the two that were done in the sake of Allah.

400
00:31:41,035 --> 00:31:42,146
The third one.

401
00:31:44,519 --> 00:31:50,464
When the king was told that there's a very beautiful woman accompanying Ibrahim عليه السّلام - Sara(سارة).

402
00:31:52,972 --> 00:31:57,992
They wanted to take away Sarah(سارة) from Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and give her as a slave to the King.

403
00:31:58,436 --> 00:32:02,055
They came to Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and they asked him: they said: Who is this woman with you?

404
00:32:02,659 --> 00:32:05,107
He said: This is my sister.

405
00:32:06,187 --> 00:32:08,274
He didn't say: She's my wife.

406
00:32:09,282 --> 00:32:12,465
If he said that she's his wife, they would kill him and take her.

407
00:32:14,020 --> 00:32:18,696
Because they don't want the husband of this woman to be alive when she's with the king.

408
00:32:19,664 --> 00:32:20,992
And then he went to Sara(سارة) and told her;

409
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:24,532
Listen; There's nobody on the face of the earth, believer, except me and you.

410
00:32:25,183 --> 00:32:27,905
And they have came and asked me, What is your relation to me?

411
00:32:27,935 --> 00:32:29,052
I said, You're my sister.

412
00:32:29,532 --> 00:32:31,469
So do not disapprove me.

413
00:32:31,810 --> 00:32:33,119
Tell them you're my sister.

414
00:32:34,024 --> 00:32:35,627
So they came to Sarah(سارة) and said;

415
00:32:36,047 --> 00:32:37,750
What is your relation with this man?

416
00:32:37,780 --> 00:32:39,061
 She said: He's my brother.

417
00:32:41,378 --> 00:32:42,672
They took Sarah(سارة).

418
00:32:44,100 --> 00:32:45,878
And they took her in to meet the king.

419
00:32:46,466 --> 00:32:48,984
And the king wanted to place his hand on her.

420
00:32:49,492 --> 00:32:51,674
She made a Dua(دُعَا) to Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

421
00:32:51,738 --> 00:32:53,746
And said: O Allah take care of him.

422
00:32:55,873 --> 00:32:57,340
His hands was paralyzed.

423
00:32:59,109 --> 00:33:06,304
So he told her: Ask your God, Ask Allah to heal me and I will leave you alone.

424
00:33:07,654 --> 00:33:10,360
So she made a Dua(دُعَا) to Allah سبحانه وتعالى to heal him.

425
00:33:10,677 --> 00:33:13,674
So his hand was moving again, he extended it again.

426
00:33:13,873 --> 00:33:16,293
He betrayed his words, he didn't keep his promise.

427
00:33:16,539 --> 00:33:19,365
She made a Dua(دُعَا) another time, his hands was paralyzed another time.

428
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:24,613
He said: Make a Dua(دُعَا) for me. She made a Dua(دُعَا) for him, a second time.

429
00:33:26,225 --> 00:33:27,510
And his hand was released.

430
00:33:28,399 --> 00:33:30,114
He tried to grab her for the third time.

431
00:33:32,019 --> 00:33:34,586
He requested the Dua(دُعَا), she made the Dua(دُعَا) for him.

432
00:33:34,753 --> 00:33:36,138
His hand was freed.

433
00:33:36,519 --> 00:33:36,876
He said;

434
00:33:36,906 --> 00:33:39,029
إنَّما جئتموني بشيطان

435
00:33:39,219 --> 00:33:42,925
You have not presented me with a human woman.

436
00:33:43,013 --> 00:33:44,835
You have presented me with a devil.

437
00:33:45,612 --> 00:33:46,700
He let her go,

438
00:33:46,882 --> 00:33:53,186
not only that, but to ward off her evil as he thought, he gave her a gift.

439
00:33:54,535 --> 00:33:58,559
He gave Sarah(سارة) a gift our mother Hajar(هَاجَر) as a slave.

440
00:33:59,734 --> 00:34:03,805
Sarah(سارة) now went back to Syedina Ibrahim(سيدنا اِبْراهِيْم) and she had this gift with her, Hajar(هَاجَر).

441
00:34:04,281 --> 00:34:07,900
And that is the story of Sayiditina Hajar(سيدتنا هَاجَر).

442
00:34:10,701 --> 00:34:16,568
In Sahi Al-Bukhari(صحيح ألبخاريْ), it mentions that Ibrahim عليه السّلام circumcised himself,

443
00:34:18,055 --> 00:34:22,464
he received the commandment of Allah سبحانه وتعالى to fulfill this Sunnah(سنة) of Fitrah(فطرة).

444
00:34:23,329 --> 00:34:26,694
And Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) did it, when he was over 80 years old.

445
00:34:28,011 --> 00:34:35,781
He circumcised himself without any anesthesia, without any painkiller, he did it himself

446
00:34:36,098 --> 00:34:40,646
immediate following of the commandments of Allah سبحانه وتعالى, even though he was over the age of 80.

447
00:34:43,110 --> 00:34:47,716
And at up to that moment, Ibrahim عليه السّلام had no children.

448
00:34:49,107 --> 00:34:55,160
He reached the age of 80, No believers, no children, leading a lonely life.

449
00:34:56,082 --> 00:34:57,477
He is patient - Sabr(صبر).

450
00:34:59,834 --> 00:35:07,721
Sarah(سارة) told Ibrahim عليه السّلام that you can have Hajar(هَاجَر) as a wife.

451
00:35:08,713 --> 00:35:11,102
Sarah(سارة) is the one, who gave Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) a permission.

452
00:35:12,802 --> 00:35:18,679
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) married Hajar(هَاجَر) with the hope that they would have a child.

453
00:35:20,965 --> 00:35:25,892
And then Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was given the Bishara(بشارة) of Ghulam Haleem(غلام حليم).

454
00:35:27,194 --> 00:35:30,946
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has described Ismail عليه السّلام with helm(حلم)

455
00:35:31,359 --> 00:35:34,414
 which is mild and gentle and forbearing.

456
00:35:35,367 --> 00:35:41,841
While Is'haq عليه السّلام has been described in Qur'an as Aleem(عليم), knowledgeable.

457
00:35:42,992 --> 00:35:49,418
So the Ayaat(آيات) that say: Ghulam Haleem(غلام حليم), a forbearing, mild, gentle child are talking about Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل)

458
00:35:49,807 --> 00:35:54,894
and the Ayaat(آيات) that say: Ghulam Aleem(غلام عليم), knowledgeable child, are the Ayaat(آيات) talking about Is'haq عليه السّلام.

459
00:35:56,196 --> 00:35:59,658
There's an interesting verse in the Bible that I want to recite to you

460
00:36:00,396 --> 00:36:06,063
because it not only gives the glad tidings of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), but it goes even further.

461
00:36:06,576 --> 00:36:09,673
This verse in the Bible is in Genesis 1720.

462
00:36:10,544 --> 00:36:16,334
It says, and as for Ismael, I have heard thee,

463
00:36:16,858 --> 00:36:24,214
Behold, I have blessed him, and will make him fruitful, and we'll multiply him exceedingly.

464
00:36:24,952 --> 00:36:29,432
12 princes, shall he beget, and I will make him a great nation.

465
00:36:31,604 --> 00:36:34,349
So the Bible is saying that Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) is blessed,

466
00:36:34,928 --> 00:36:40,883
and that Allah سبحانه وتعالى will multiply his children and his children are the Arabs

467
00:36:41,637 --> 00:36:47,494
and 12 princes, out of the descendants of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) will be 12 princes.

468
00:36:48,574 --> 00:36:51,939
There is a Hadith(حديث) where Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

469
00:36:52,462 --> 00:36:58,733
There will be on this Ummah(امة) twelve(12) Khulafaa(خلفاء) all of them are from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

470
00:37:00,204 --> 00:37:00,905
12.

471
00:37:01,641 --> 00:37:04,867
And Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are from the direct descendants of  Ismael عليه السّلام.

472
00:37:05,779 --> 00:37:08,542
And this verse in the Bible is talking about 12 princes

473
00:37:08,906 --> 00:37:11,382
and the 12 princes are 12 Khulafaa(خلفاء).

474
00:37:12,382 --> 00:37:17,475
Four of them are already past Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر), Uthman(عثمان) and Ali(علي).

475
00:37:17,879 --> 00:37:24,065
Some would include Umar Bin Abdel Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز), for sure we know about the four and then Al-Mahdi(ألمهدي) is one also.

476
00:37:24,192 --> 00:37:26,168
And there are a few others left.

477
00:37:27,438 --> 00:37:31,039
Not only is the Bible giving us the glad tidings of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل),

478
00:37:31,069 --> 00:37:35,323
but it's also talking about the 12 Khulafaa(خلفاء) that will rule on this Ummah(امة).

479
00:37:35,633 --> 00:37:40,371
If we have only four or five or six of the Khulafaa(خلفاء) that passed

480
00:37:40,752 --> 00:37:44,988
we have more than half left and that's the good news for this Ummah(امة).

481
00:37:46,329 --> 00:37:52,560
In Fath-Al-Bari(فتح الباري), the commentary of Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ) by Imam Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(إمام إبن حجر ألعسقلاني), he says that

482
00:37:52,655 --> 00:38:01,833
when Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) carried his young child and Hajar(هَاجَر) in their Hijrah(هجرة), Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) was about two years old of age.

483
00:38:03,968 --> 00:38:09,397
Ibrahim عليه السّلام commanded his wife Hajar(هَاجَر) to accompany him in a long trip.

484
00:38:11,127 --> 00:38:17,779
So they started this long traveling, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and his wife Hajar(هَاجَر) and their young child Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل).

485
00:38:18,071 --> 00:38:26,361
And then suddenly in the middle of nowhere, desert, dry, barren in fertile desert,

486
00:38:26,676 --> 00:38:34,212
no settlements, no people, no houses, no villages, nothing in the middle of nowhere Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) stopped

487
00:38:36,136 --> 00:38:38,644
and he told his wife Hazel and her son to stay there.

488
00:38:40,239 --> 00:38:44,426
And he left with them a sack filled with dates.

489
00:38:45,783 --> 00:38:47,117
And he left to them some water.

490
00:38:47,815 --> 00:38:51,738
Hajar(هَاجَر) couldn't believe what's happening.

491
00:38:53,516 --> 00:38:59,310
How could we be left over here in the middle of nowhere desert?

492
00:38:59,659 --> 00:39:01,762
So, she followed Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

493
00:39:02,016 --> 00:39:03,389
Are you going to leave us here?

494
00:39:04,183 --> 00:39:05,715
Who are you going to leave us with?

495
00:39:06,421 --> 00:39:09,134
There's no plants, there's no people, there's nothing.

496
00:39:09,840 --> 00:39:11,483
Who are you going to leave us with?

497
00:39:12,362 --> 00:39:15,926
And Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was not answering, and he's walking away, he didn't even look back.

498
00:39:17,569 --> 00:39:20,323
And she repeated the question Who are you going to leave us with?

499
00:39:21,410 --> 00:39:22,435
He's walking away.

500
00:39:23,070 --> 00:39:24,145
She's following him.

501
00:39:24,391 --> 00:39:29,364
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), how are you going to leave us here, there's nothing here there's no people.

502
00:39:30,054 --> 00:39:33,387
And Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was completely ignoring her and not even looking back.

503
00:39:34,038 --> 00:39:36,055
Then finally she asked him a question.

504
00:39:37,039 --> 00:39:41,666
She said: Is this a commandment from Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

505
00:39:43,438 --> 00:39:48,089
Finally, Ibrahim عليه السّلام responded and said: Yes.

506
00:39:49,438 --> 00:39:51,083
Sayidit'na Hajar(سيدتنا هاجر) said;

507
00:39:51,113 --> 00:39:53,258
إذن لن يضيعن الله

508
00:39:53,599 --> 00:39:56,486
Then Allah سبحانه وتعالى will not neglect us.

509
00:39:56,797 --> 00:39:57,265
That's it.

510
00:39:57,424 --> 00:39:59,098
She didn't talk with him further.

511
00:40:00,144 --> 00:40:02,025
Allah told you to do this? Yes.

512
00:40:02,231 --> 00:40:05,906
Allah سبحانه وتعالى will take care of us, He will not neglect us.

513
00:40:07,477 --> 00:40:13,174
This is the Eeman(ايمان) of this mother - Hajar(هَاجَر) - the mother of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

514
00:40:13,666 --> 00:40:15,229
This is her Eeman(ايمان).

515
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:20,999
She's in the desert, dry desert, no one is there.

516
00:40:22,205 --> 00:40:23,917
She doesn't even have enough food.

517
00:40:23,977 --> 00:40:29,294
All what she have is dates and water, something that we would complain about.

518
00:40:30,271 --> 00:40:35,056
If we're told to live on for one day not to make a living off water on dates.

519
00:40:37,282 --> 00:40:40,782
And her husband is leaving her alone, a helpless mother.

520
00:40:42,155 --> 00:40:47,078
Hajar(هَاجَر) sat down, she would breastfeed him and she would eat from that dates.

521
00:40:47,387 --> 00:40:52,903
Drink from the water, until she ran out of dates and ran out of water and ran out of milk.

522
00:40:54,514 --> 00:40:58,693
Now Syedina Ismail عليه السّلام is crying and weeping

523
00:40:59,241 --> 00:41:01,289
and Rasool Allah ﷺ described him and said;

524
00:41:01,339 --> 00:41:02,336
 يتلوَّأ

525
00:41:02,622 --> 00:41:03,930
He was curling.

526
00:41:04,477 --> 00:41:07,468
Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) was curling on himself because of the hunger.

527
00:41:08,055 --> 00:41:10,865
And he was hitting the ground with his feet.

528
00:41:11,553 --> 00:41:13,990
And he was crying as if he was dying.

529
00:41:15,204 --> 00:41:17,823
At that moment, Hajar(هَاجَر) could not sit down any further.

530
00:41:20,014 --> 00:41:25,401
Even though there's nowhere to go, but she couldn't handle seeing her child dying in front of her eyes.

531
00:41:26,822 --> 00:41:31,417
So she went on top of a mountain that was close to her, she climbed that mountain.

532
00:41:34,552 --> 00:41:36,015
And that mountain was As-Suffa(ألصفاء)

533
00:41:37,769 --> 00:41:40,515
and she looks on top of the mountain if she can see anyone.

534
00:41:40,920 --> 00:41:42,182
She saw no one.

535
00:41:43,079 --> 00:41:47,431
She walk down the mountain, and then she ran through the valley.

536
00:41:47,582 --> 00:41:49,288
And then she climbed another mountain.

537
00:41:50,606 --> 00:41:52,510
The name of that mountain is Al-Marwa(ألمروة).

538
00:41:53,661 --> 00:41:58,645
She got to the top of the mountain, looking around if she can see anyone she saw no one.

539
00:41:59,272 --> 00:42:04,393
So she was down the mountain ran through the valley climbed on As-Suffa(ألصفاء) again.

540
00:42:06,060 --> 00:42:09,520
And she kept on doing that for seven times.

541
00:42:12,401 --> 00:42:16,356
And that is the Sunnah(سنة) of Sayiditna Hajar(سيدتناهَاجَر) that we are doing today in Hajj(حَجْ).

542
00:42:16,386 --> 00:42:17,967
Every one of us is making that site.

543
00:42:20,777 --> 00:42:28,139
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Sayiditna Hajar(سيدتناهَاجَر) at that moment, was afraid, had fear in her heart, she was running with worry.

544
00:42:28,774 --> 00:42:33,180
If she knew what will happen, she would be climbing those mountains with a big smile on her face.

545
00:42:34,109 --> 00:42:40,528
If she knew that the nations of the world, millions and millions of them are going to follow her tracks

546
00:42:41,281 --> 00:42:47,014
and follow her Sunnah(سنة) and follow her way, she would be making that trip with a big smile on her face.

547
00:42:47,594 --> 00:42:52,022
And this is the Rizq(رزق) that Allah سبحانه وتعالى gives to you from the doors that you don't expect.

548
00:42:52,276 --> 00:42:56,343
وَمَن يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجعَل لَهُ مَخرَجًا۝وَيَرزُقهُ مِن حَيثُ لا يَحتَسِبُ ۚ

549
00:42:56,636 --> 00:42:59,001
If you have Taqwa(تقوى) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى,

550
00:42:59,351 --> 00:43:04,009
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى will provide for you Rizq(رزق) from places you never expect.

551
00:43:04,374 --> 00:43:08,985
When she got on top of Al-Marwa(ألمروة), and that's the end of the seventh showed, the seventh climbing.

552
00:43:09,882 --> 00:43:11,065
She heard the voice.

553
00:43:12,001 --> 00:43:14,972
She said - ساة - quite,

554
00:43:15,112 --> 00:43:15,987
 who she's speaking to.

555
00:43:16,145 --> 00:43:18,050
She's speaking to herself out of confusion.

556
00:43:18,693 --> 00:43:20,701
She's telling herself, Be quiet.

557
00:43:21,598 --> 00:43:22,786
And then is trying to listen.

558
00:43:24,199 --> 00:43:25,667
She heard the voice again, she said;

559
00:43:25,697 --> 00:43:27,921
لقد أسمعت إن كان لديك غواة

560
00:43:28,222 --> 00:43:31,076
If you have any help, I'm able to hear you. Where are you?

561
00:43:31,945 --> 00:43:38,486
And then she looked around to see in the spot where Ismael عليه السّلام was laying down.

562
00:43:39,164 --> 00:43:45,866
The child, the two year old child, the helpless child, the child that is crying, helpless.

563
00:43:46,398 --> 00:43:53,006
She saw an angel, leader of the angels, Jibreel عليه السّلام descended, especially

564
00:43:54,157 --> 00:43:57,257
 to that spot where Ismael عليه السّلام was laying down

565
00:43:57,884 --> 00:44:05,456
and Angel started picking up, the dirt with his wink or with his foot, until water started flowing from the ground.

566
00:44:07,146 --> 00:44:11,981
Rizq(رزق) of Allah that came for a helpless child.

567
00:44:13,323 --> 00:44:15,577
So she came down, Sayiditna Hajar(سيدتناهَاجَر).

568
00:44:16,847 --> 00:44:22,257
This water of Zam-Zam(زمزم) came out through divine will of Allah سبحانه وتعالى

569
00:44:23,138 --> 00:44:25,297
 a commandment to the angel Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل),

570
00:44:26,123 --> 00:44:29,558
 when the water was coming out with the will of Allah سبحانه وتعالى

571
00:44:29,732 --> 00:44:36,708
Sayiditna Hajar(سيدتناهَاجَر) intervene by making a pool around the water.

572
00:44:37,520 --> 00:44:39,623
Because this water was coming out in a desert,

573
00:44:40,695 --> 00:44:47,393
so she thought that this water is gonna flow on the sand and go into Earth and she's not gonna see it.

574
00:44:47,703 --> 00:44:51,363
She intervenes and she started saying them Zam-Zam(زمزم), Zam-Zam(زمزم)

575
00:44:51,538 --> 00:44:54,498
and she's collecting dirt around it to make a pool.

576
00:44:55,704 --> 00:45:02,400
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: If Hajar(هَاجَر) would have left it alone, it would have been a flowing river.

577
00:45:03,979 --> 00:45:09,226
She intervened in it, if she would have left alone it would have been a flowing river,

578
00:45:09,440 --> 00:45:14,138
but she intervene and it became the well of Zam-Zam(زمزم).

579
00:45:17,702 --> 00:45:20,018
Now Sayiditna Hajar(سيدتناهَاجَر) has water,

580
00:45:20,405 --> 00:45:23,167
but she doesn't have food, and she doesn't have company.

581
00:45:23,405 --> 00:45:28,333
So she still needs the social needs and psychological needs.

582
00:45:31,444 --> 00:45:37,610
There was a tribe called Jurhum(جرهم), an Arab tribe, Bedouins traveling in that area.

583
00:45:40,316 --> 00:45:49,354
They saw in the sky, birds hovering, birds in the desert means water.

584
00:45:50,005 --> 00:45:54,550
They said: We know that there's no water over there. So what are these birds doing?

585
00:45:56,526 --> 00:45:58,145
فارسلو جريً أو جريين

586
00:45:58,175 --> 00:46:01,530
All of this that I'm mentioning to you is from long Hadith(حديث) in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

587
00:46:03,038 --> 00:46:05,784
So they sent one or two men to go and investigate.

588
00:46:07,125 --> 00:46:08,411
So the men went rushing.

589
00:46:09,109 --> 00:46:12,442
They came back with the good news that there's water in the middle of the desert,

590
00:46:13,022 --> 00:46:18,701
this group of Jurhum(جرهم), they moved towards the source of water.

591
00:46:19,502 --> 00:46:24,391
And they came there, they arrived there to find this woman and her child.

592
00:46:24,843 --> 00:46:30,368
So they asked a strange question and they got an even stranger answer.

593
00:46:32,757 --> 00:46:38,124
Their question was, would you allow us to camp here?

594
00:46:39,354 --> 00:46:41,275
Would you allow us to camp here?

595
00:46:41,846 --> 00:46:43,139
What is strange about this?

596
00:46:44,734 --> 00:46:52,925
These are a group of men, fighters in the middle of the desert, taking permission from a woman and her child.

597
00:46:54,655 --> 00:46:59,314
If they wanted, they could have eliminated her with a move of a hand.

598
00:46:59,854 --> 00:47:03,020
With a strike of a sword, she could have been over with.

599
00:47:04,600 --> 00:47:06,997
But they were very noble.

600
00:47:07,377 --> 00:47:12,023
So they came and asked her that strange question, would you give us permission to stay here?

601
00:47:12,799 --> 00:47:15,404
Because in the desert, if you have water, that's where you want to be.

602
00:47:17,412 --> 00:47:18,625
And they got a strange answer.

603
00:47:18,655 --> 00:47:19,396
She said;

604
00:47:20,435 --> 00:47:25,203
Yes! But you have no rights in the water, the water belongs to us.

605
00:47:26,489 --> 00:47:28,338
And what's strange about that answer,

606
00:47:28,656 --> 00:47:33,301
the strange thing about it, is that she is in no position to negotiate and bargain.

607
00:47:34,967 --> 00:47:38,944
And nevertheless she is saying;

608
00:47:39,260 --> 00:47:43,837
You have no right in the water, if you want to stay here, you have to stay on our terms, the water belongs to us.

609
00:47:45,799 --> 00:47:48,638
But they accepted, they said: Yes, we agree.

610
00:47:50,186 --> 00:47:52,978
And that is how Jurhum(جرهم) came to stay in that area.

611
00:47:53,478 --> 00:47:55,367
And this is the beginning of the settlement.

612
00:47:57,018 --> 00:48:04,726
Now let me go back when Ibrahim عليه السّلام left Hajar(هَاجَر) and her son in that spot.

613
00:48:05,766 --> 00:48:09,337
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) walked away, until he got to As-Saniya(ألثنية).

614
00:48:09,837 --> 00:48:11,093
And he made Dua(دُعَا) for them.

615
00:48:11,482 --> 00:48:22,152
It's not easy for a father, very old to leave his only son and his wife in the middle of nowhere, it's not easy.

616
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:30,980
We do not feel safe leaving our families alone in settled, established secure areas.

617
00:48:31,654 --> 00:48:33,587
It wasn't easy for Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) to leave.

618
00:48:34,126 --> 00:48:37,744
So he stopped and made Dua(دُعَا) to Allah because that is who we seek help from.

619
00:48:37,774 --> 00:48:39,489
إِيّاكَ نَعبُدُ وَإِيّاكَ نَستَعينُ۝

620
00:48:39,519 --> 00:48:41,280
We seek help from no-one but Allah.

621
00:48:42,378 --> 00:48:43,823
And he made a Dua(دُعَا).

622
00:48:44,434 --> 00:48:45,902
What was the Dua(دُعَا) of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

623
00:48:46,156 --> 00:48:46,616
He said;

624
00:48:46,711 --> 00:48:54,466
رَبَّنا إِنّي أَسكَنتُ مِن ذُرِّيَّتي بِوادٍ

625
00:48:54,568 --> 00:49:00,164
 بِوادٍ غَيرِ ذي زَرعٍ عِندَ بَيتِكَ المُحَرَّمِ

626
00:49:00,194 --> 00:49:08,407
رَبَّنا لِيُقيمُوا الصَّلاةَ فَاجعَل أَفئِدَةً مِنَ النّاسِ تَهوي إِلَيهِم

627
00:49:08,589 --> 00:49:21,388
 فَاجعَل أَفئِدَةً مِنَ النّاسِ تَهوي إِلَيهِم وَارزُقهُم مِنَ الثَّمَراتِ لَعَلَّهُم يَشكُرونَ۝

628
00:49:21,418 --> 00:49:34,409
O Allah; I have left my descendant, my family in a valley that is barren and dry in fertile no rain, no trees can grow in that place.

629
00:49:35,337 --> 00:49:36,218
Why?

630
00:49:37,552 --> 00:49:39,131
 لِيُقيمُوا الصَّلاةَ

631
00:49:39,409 --> 00:49:41,861
so that they may establish prayer.

632
00:49:44,242 --> 00:49:56,153
In that moment of difficulty, in that moment which we would naturally think about the safety and the food and the drink of my child and my wife,

633
00:49:56,471 --> 00:49:58,751
Ibrahim عليه السّلام is thinking about Salah(صلاة).

634
00:49:59,831 --> 00:50:06,126
Something similar to it because the Sahabah(صحابه) are trained under the head of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) Muhammadﷺ.

635
00:50:06,277 --> 00:50:08,690
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was talking about Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال)

636
00:50:09,428 --> 00:50:12,428
 and Rasool Ullah said that the Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال) will remain among you for 40 days.

637
00:50:12,674 --> 00:50:16,610
One day is equal to a year, one day is equal to a month and then, one day is equal to week,

638
00:50:16,844 --> 00:50:19,122
 and the rest of the days are like your regular days.

639
00:50:20,257 --> 00:50:23,448
So one day is equal to a year, the Sahabah(صحابه) had a question about that.

640
00:50:24,321 --> 00:50:27,305
One day is equal to a year what do you think their question was?

641
00:50:28,313 --> 00:50:30,709
I mean, Rasool Ullah was talking about the big Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال)

642
00:50:31,368 --> 00:50:33,757
and he's talking about a day that is equal to a year.

643
00:50:34,177 --> 00:50:36,870
What is the thought that came on the minds of the Sahabah(صحابه)

644
00:50:36,900 --> 00:50:37,248
they said;

645
00:50:37,278 --> 00:50:39,152
هل تكفينا فيه صلاة اليوم

646
00:50:39,319 --> 00:50:42,420
Is it enough for us to pray in that day like this prayer of one day.

647
00:50:42,571 --> 00:50:47,317
The Sahabah(صحابه) are thinking about Salah(صلاة) in the time of Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال).

648
00:50:47,460 --> 00:50:48,939
Rasool Ullah is talking about Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال)

649
00:50:48,969 --> 00:50:51,860
and the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال) and the Sahabah(صحابه) are thinking about Salah(صلاة).

650
00:50:52,328 --> 00:50:53,336
Anyway Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said;

651
00:50:53,366 --> 00:50:54,082
لِيُقيمُوا الصَّلاةَ

652
00:50:54,112 --> 00:50:59,115
so that they would establish prayer and then he made the Dua(دُعَا) of the other needs.

653
00:50:59,805 --> 00:51:03,543
We're not saying we don't seek assistance from Allah, to give us Rizq(رزق). No;

654
00:51:04,083 --> 00:51:07,639
We don't say that we don't seek assistance from Allah to provide for us in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا). No;

655
00:51:07,972 --> 00:51:09,242
We ask Allah for that.

656
00:51:09,790 --> 00:51:12,395
But we have to give right proportion,

657
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:15,149
"رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً"

658
00:51:15,665 --> 00:51:17,760
We asked Allah for Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and we ask Allah for Aakhirah(آخِرة).

659
00:51:17,990 --> 00:51:22,920
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) mentioned the duty of Islam and that is the establishment of Salah(صلاة)

660
00:51:22,950 --> 00:51:23,904
and then he said;

661
00:51:25,269 --> 00:51:30,003
فَاجعَل أَفئِدَةً مِنَ النّاسِ تَهوي إِلَيهِم وَارزُقهُم مِنَ الثَّمَراتِ لَعَلَّهُم يَشكُرونَ۝

662
00:51:30,519 --> 00:51:36,511
So make flocks of people love them and come to them and provide from them fruits.

663
00:51:37,399 --> 00:51:42,465
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) that Dua(دُعَا) that was done in the desert, in the empty desert.

664
00:51:43,203 --> 00:51:46,751
Look at the fulfillment of the Dua(دُعَا) of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

665
00:51:47,751 --> 00:51:50,195
People are coming from all over the world to that place.

666
00:51:51,291 --> 00:51:53,602
There is no place in the world that is more loved than Makkah.

667
00:51:55,063 --> 00:51:59,939
Because of the attraction that Allah سبحانه وتعالى put in that house.

668
00:52:01,129 --> 00:52:06,740
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given an amazing description to the house of Allah.

669
00:52:07,351 --> 00:52:08,207
Allah says;

670
00:52:08,492 --> 00:52:11,151
وَإِذْ جَعَلْنَا الْبَيْتَ مَثَابَةً لِلنَّاسِ

671
00:52:11,778 --> 00:52:21,876
Masaba(مَثَابَةً), when the young camel goes to play after it plays for a while it has to go back and see its mother.

672
00:52:23,741 --> 00:52:28,310
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى says that the house of Allah is Masaba(مَثَابَةً) you go there, you get stuck.

673
00:52:29,643 --> 00:52:35,922
The love of the house of Allah enters your heart and then when you leave from Makkah, you're always homesick.

674
00:52:36,985 --> 00:52:39,731
You want to go back and see Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) again.

675
00:52:40,422 --> 00:52:42,533
And that is something that many people describe.

676
00:52:43,033 --> 00:52:43,547
They say that

677
00:52:43,577 --> 00:52:50,816
when we see Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) for the first time, then that's it, we're hooked to it and we can't leave it for a long time.

678
00:52:51,580 --> 00:52:57,782
Allah سبحانه وتعالى puts the love of this house in the hearts of men, a fulfillment of the Dua(دُعَا) of Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

679
00:52:59,004 --> 00:53:01,131
So the people of Jurhum(جرهم) they stayed there.

680
00:53:01,481 --> 00:53:04,909
And they raised up Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) and they taught him the Arabic language.

681
00:53:05,489 --> 00:53:12,097
Because Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was not an Arab neither was Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), they were from Mesopotamia - in Iraq - the Caledonians.

682
00:53:13,557 --> 00:53:17,633
Jurhum(جرهم), they taught Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) the Arabic language because he grew up with them.

683
00:53:17,768 --> 00:53:19,625
So he learned the Arabic language,

684
00:53:20,562 --> 00:53:21,411
 فاَنفسهم

685
00:53:21,441 --> 00:53:24,915
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: They adored him, they loved him so much.

686
00:53:25,653 --> 00:53:29,368
They married him one of their daughters, and he lived with them.

687
00:53:30,407 --> 00:53:32,824
The mother passed away Hajar(هَاجَر).

688
00:53:33,356 --> 00:53:36,070
And then Ibrahim عليه السّلام would make some visits.

689
00:53:36,308 --> 00:53:38,108
Ibrahim عليه السّلام is traveling always.

690
00:53:38,312 --> 00:53:48,239
So he visited Makkah and he came to the house of Ismail عليه السّلام and he knocked the door.

691
00:53:50,016 --> 00:53:51,620
So, his wife opened the door.

692
00:53:51,848 --> 00:53:54,784
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said: Where's your husband?

693
00:53:54,814 --> 00:53:57,634
She said: He's, he's not here.

694
00:53:58,737 --> 00:54:01,320
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) asked her: How is your living?

695
00:54:01,891 --> 00:54:03,153
She said: Miserable.

696
00:54:03,987 --> 00:54:07,633
We're having a miserable life, and she complained.

697
00:54:08,061 --> 00:54:14,294
Our food is not good our water is murky and thick and dirty, salty.

698
00:54:14,935 --> 00:54:17,046
So Ibrahim عليه السّلام said;

699
00:54:19,015 --> 00:54:23,001
فأقرئي منِّي السلام، وقولي له: يغير عتبة باب

700
00:54:24,255 --> 00:54:28,067
Deliver my Salaams to him, he didn't even tell her, who he is.

701
00:54:28,178 --> 00:54:33,004
He said: Deliver my Salam to him and tell him to change his doorstep.

702
00:54:34,996 --> 00:54:39,141
Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) came home and Rasool Allah ﷺ says: As if he felt something.

703
00:54:39,171 --> 00:54:42,753
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) he felt that his father was there.

704
00:54:42,864 --> 00:54:44,988
He didn't see him and his wife, she didn't even say anything,

705
00:54:45,083 --> 00:54:47,306
and he asked his wife, did anybody visit us?

706
00:54:47,797 --> 00:54:51,536
She said: Yes. An old man came and he asked about you.

707
00:54:52,437 --> 00:54:58,802
And he told me to deliver Salaam to you and to tell you to change your doorstep.

708
00:54:59,929 --> 00:55:07,521
Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) said that was my father and he's ordering me to separate from you, you're the doorstep.

709
00:55:08,069 --> 00:55:11,288
So go back home! And he divorced her.

710
00:55:12,176 --> 00:55:18,663
People of Jurhum(جرهم) they loved Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) so much, they married him another wife.

711
00:55:21,679 --> 00:55:23,163
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) made another trip.

712
00:55:23,489 --> 00:55:27,142
A while later, knocked the door Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) wasn't there.

713
00:55:27,172 --> 00:55:29,261
So he asked the same questions to the wife.

714
00:55:29,291 --> 00:55:31,820
He said; Tell me about your living.

715
00:55:31,880 --> 00:55:34,353
She said: Al-hamdulillah(ألحمدلله), the best living.

716
00:55:35,631 --> 00:55:43,493
and she praised the lifestyle that they're leading, this simple lifestyle that they were leading, she praised it.

717
00:55:43,786 --> 00:55:45,112
She was happy and content;

718
00:55:45,421 --> 00:55:46,096
 أمراة صالحة

719
00:55:46,126 --> 00:55:47,104
 righteous woman.

720
00:55:48,707 --> 00:55:50,409
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) wanted to get more details.

721
00:55:50,439 --> 00:55:51,584
He said: What food do you eat?

722
00:55:51,735 --> 00:55:52,933
She said: We eat meat.

723
00:55:53,600 --> 00:55:55,155
What do you drink? Water.

724
00:55:55,909 --> 00:56:03,767
That's all what they used to have meat and water, no desserts, no appetizers, no side dish, meat and water only.

725
00:56:05,497 --> 00:56:09,160
So he made Dua(دُعَا) for them and said Allah gives them blessing in their food.

726
00:56:09,723 --> 00:56:14,914
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says they did not have grains at that time they did not know wheat and barley.

727
00:56:15,112 --> 00:56:21,164
If they had it, he would have made Dua(دُعَا) for them, to bless it for them, but he didn't have it at that time.

728
00:56:21,736 --> 00:56:24,539
But he may Dua(دُعَا) to Allah to bless for them, their food.

729
00:56:25,563 --> 00:56:32,942
And then he said: When your husband, comes back, deliver my salaam to him, and tell him to keep the doorstep.

730
00:56:34,720 --> 00:56:36,616
So Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) came back.

731
00:56:36,735 --> 00:56:38,022
He said: Did anybody visit us?

732
00:56:38,052 --> 00:56:42,527
He said: Yes, an old man came and he's delivering your salaam(سلام) and he is saying; keep your doorstep.

733
00:56:42,587 --> 00:56:48,059
He said that's my father. You are the doorstep and my father is telling me, to keep you.

734
00:56:51,674 --> 00:56:54,388
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

735
00:56:54,729 --> 00:56:55,979
رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ۝

736
00:56:56,009 --> 00:56:57,890
This is a Dua(دُعَا) that's Sayidina Ibrahim(سيدنا اِبْراهِيْم) made.

737
00:56:58,010 --> 00:56:59,445
  رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ۝

738
00:56:59,652 --> 00:57:03,225
 O Allah سبحانه وتعالى give me an a righteous offspring.

739
00:57:03,543 --> 00:57:13,259
Ibrahim عليه السّلام reached to over 80 years old and he didn't have any offspring, he didn't have any children.

740
00:57:15,529 --> 00:57:18,825
And he didn't ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى to provide him with children per say

741
00:57:18,878 --> 00:57:22,061
but he said: Minas Saliheen(من الصالحين) he has to be righteous.

742
00:57:22,974 --> 00:57:26,627
O Allah سبحانه وتعالى give me an a righteous offspring.

743
00:57:28,429 --> 00:57:29,421
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

744
00:57:29,476 --> 00:57:33,055
فَبَشَّرناهُ بِغُلامٍ حَليمٍ۝

745
00:57:33,085 --> 00:57:38,791
We gave him the glad tidings of a child, which is Haleem(حليم).

746
00:57:39,752 --> 00:57:44,065
And Haleem(حليم) is gentle and mild and forbearing.

747
00:57:44,724 --> 00:57:49,447
These are the Akhlaq(أخلاق) of Syedina Ismael عليه السّلام

748
00:57:49,939 --> 00:57:56,256
and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) grew up away from his father, in Makkah as we mentioned.

749
00:57:58,158 --> 00:58:02,538
And then when Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) reached to the age

750
00:58:03,316 --> 00:58:09,812
in which he can go out with his father in the age in which he became an adult,

751
00:58:10,304 --> 00:58:13,939
and is able to take responsibilities for himself.

752
00:58:15,447 --> 00:58:18,092
This age which Allah سبحانه وتعالى mentions in Qur'an.

753
00:58:18,122 --> 00:58:20,092
فَلَمّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعيَ

754
00:58:21,029 --> 00:58:28,031
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says and when his son was old enough to walk with him.

755
00:58:29,579 --> 00:58:38,253
Means that Ismail عليه السّلام has grew up and now is able to take care of himself and he's able to take responsibilities.

756
00:58:40,298 --> 00:58:45,736
And that is when the father starts seeing himself in his son.

757
00:58:47,197 --> 00:58:49,955
When your son is a child, you raised him up,

758
00:58:50,170 --> 00:58:55,643
but when your son is an adult, then you see the continuation of your life in him

759
00:58:55,927 --> 00:59:00,974
and that is the age which is Ismael عليه السّلام reached.

760
00:59:03,067 --> 00:59:05,992
When Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) started to go out with his father.

761
00:59:06,063 --> 00:59:08,611
Sayidina Ibrahim عليه السّلام saw dream.

762
00:59:09,603 --> 00:59:15,021
Sayidina Ibrahim(سيدنااِبْراهِيْم) saw a dream and we know that the dreams of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) are Wahii(وحي).

763
00:59:18,672 --> 00:59:23,297
In that dream Sayidina Ibrahim(سيدنااِبْراهِيْم) was slaughtering his own son.

764
00:59:25,266 --> 00:59:39,520
فَلَمّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعيَ قالَ يا بُنَيَّ إِنّي أَرىٰ فِي المَنامِ أَنّي أَذبَحُكَ فَانظُر ماذا تَرىٰ ۚ

765
00:59:39,550 --> 00:59:44,211
Oh my son I see in my dream that I am sacrificing you.

766
00:59:45,338 --> 00:59:46,481
 فَانظُر ماذا تَرىٰ ۚ

767
00:59:46,679 --> 00:59:50,695
What do you think, what is your response?

768
00:59:51,632 --> 00:59:56,386
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) he will fulfill the order of Allah سبحانه وتعالى no doubt,

769
00:59:57,005 --> 01:00:03,681
but he didn't go and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) is in his Sleep and suddenly sacrifices his son.

770
01:00:03,856 --> 01:00:05,693
No, he told Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), he said;

771
01:00:05,769 --> 01:00:08,225
 This is the dream that I saw telling me what do you think?

772
01:00:08,328 --> 01:00:19,308
The answer of Sayidina Ismael عليه السّلام should be studied deeply and taken seriously, by the society that we live in.

773
01:00:20,832 --> 01:00:25,065
This society that gives no rights to the parents

774
01:00:25,279 --> 01:00:31,157
in which the children have no morals in the way they deal with their parents

775
01:00:32,538 --> 01:00:37,038
and in the society that would give rights to everyone even to the perverted

776
01:00:38,157 --> 01:00:40,369
but it would give no rights to the parents.

777
01:00:41,599 --> 01:00:45,798
In a society where the state has more authority over your children than you do.

778
01:00:47,290 --> 01:00:50,453
This response of Sayidina Ismail(سيدنااِسْماعِيْل) needs to be studied very carefully.

779
01:00:50,659 --> 01:00:52,786
Sayidina Ismael عليه السّلام said;

780
01:00:52,921 --> 01:01:03,248
قالَ يا أَبَتِ افعَل ما تُؤمَرُ ۖ سَتَجِدُني إِن شاءَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الصّابِرينَ۝

781
01:01:03,278 --> 01:01:06,661
 O my father, do what you are commanded to do.

782
01:01:07,130 --> 01:01:13,214
If a parent will tell his child to provide for him, the son or the daughter won't.

783
01:01:15,015 --> 01:01:19,074
And in the end of their life, they're dumped in an elderly house

784
01:01:20,764 --> 01:01:26,631
and Sayidina Ismael عليه السّلام is giving the most valuable thing that he has and that is his life.

785
01:01:27,258 --> 01:01:34,892
It's not a matter of providing for his father material provisions or taking care of some needs of his father.

786
01:01:35,115 --> 01:01:38,377
He's giving his father his life, he's giving away his life.

787
01:01:38,575 --> 01:01:42,686
And again, I say that's important to study by us, the Muslims,

788
01:01:42,908 --> 01:01:47,416
because we are living in a society that gives no rights to parents.

789
01:01:47,476 --> 01:01:49,726
The only group that have no rights are the parents.

790
01:01:50,281 --> 01:01:51,924
They have no rights whatsoever.

791
01:01:52,559 --> 01:01:57,553
They're disposable thing, they just raise up the children, they bear them and they take care of them

792
01:01:57,831 --> 01:02:04,695
and they work for them and they sacrifice for them, and then when the children reach the age of 18,

793
01:02:05,172 --> 01:02:09,830
they have no obligation whatsoever towards these parents, and that is by law.

794
01:02:11,227 --> 01:02:17,697
The parent cannot take anything from their children after they reach the age of 18, by law, nothing.

795
01:02:20,530 --> 01:02:25,811
The child does not have to obey, does not have to provide does not have to take care

796
01:02:26,065 --> 01:02:28,557
because it's an individualistic society.

797
01:02:29,383 --> 01:02:35,724
And it's affecting the Muslims, it's affecting us because we borrow from the environment we live in.

798
01:02:36,994 --> 01:02:40,270
Sayidina Ismail(سيدنااِسْماعِيْل) said do whatever you are commanded to do.

799
01:02:40,300 --> 01:02:41,064
  افعَل ما تُؤمَرُ ۖ

800
01:02:41,120 --> 01:02:45,143
Do whatever you're told to do, whatever Allah commanded you to do; Do it.

801
01:02:45,818 --> 01:02:46,593
And then he said;

802
01:02:46,723 --> 01:02:50,552
سَتَجِدُني إِن شاءَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الصّابِرينَ۝

803
01:02:50,973 --> 01:02:55,116
You will find me of those, who are patient In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله).

804
01:02:56,330 --> 01:03:01,358
He didn’t say you will find me patient because we cannot guarantee our actions,

805
01:03:01,715 --> 01:03:06,096
we have no guarantee over what we're going to do this moment, let alone in the future.

806
01:03:06,636 --> 01:03:10,576
Everything that we do we need to realize that it's Taufeeq(توفيق) from Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

807
01:03:11,449 --> 01:03:14,290
Allah is the One, Who made it accessible for us.

808
01:03:15,274 --> 01:03:21,509
And that is why we don't say that we're going to do it and put an end to it that way.

809
01:03:21,539 --> 01:03:23,596
No, we said: We're going to do it In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله).

810
01:03:23,874 --> 01:03:26,902
And we asked Allah سبحانه وتعالى to assist us in doing so.

811
01:03:27,283 --> 01:03:28,951
And that is why in every Salah(صلاة) we say;

812
01:03:28,981 --> 01:03:30,164
أهدنا الصراط المستقيم

813
01:03:30,194 --> 01:03:32,965
Guide us to the straight path, it's You, Who will guide us.

814
01:03:33,712 --> 01:03:37,800
Without Your help, we cannot do anything, without Your help, we cannot worship You.

815
01:03:39,657 --> 01:03:45,917
And that's why we need to thank Allah سبحانه وتعالى for every good deed that we do,

816
01:03:46,044 --> 01:03:49,425
and then we need to thank Allah سبحانه وتعالى because he allowed us to thank Him.

817
01:03:51,687 --> 01:03:53,816
سَتَجِدُني إِن شاءَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الصّابِرينَ۝

818
01:03:56,181 --> 01:03:57,554
And then Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

819
01:03:57,642 --> 01:04:02,944
فَلَمّا أَسلَما وَتَلَّهُ لِلجَبينِ۝

820
01:04:02,974 --> 01:04:10,602
Then, when they both submitted themselves and he had laid him on his forehead,

821
01:04:13,481 --> 01:04:20,199
the position Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) was in, he was laying on the ground, and his father was holding the knife over his neck.

822
01:04:21,366 --> 01:04:24,739
When they were in that position, Allah سبحانه وتعالى described it as follows,

823
01:04:24,874 --> 01:04:30,067
فَلَمّا أَسلَما وَتَلَّهُ لِلجَبينِ۝

824
01:04:30,097 --> 01:04:32,043
 When they both submitted

825
01:04:33,614 --> 01:04:38,118
and the word Aslama(أسلما) and Islam(إسلام) comes from the same root,

826
01:04:39,904 --> 01:04:44,574
the root of the word Aslama(أسلما) and Islam(إسلام) is the same thing.

827
01:04:46,510 --> 01:04:50,154
Allah سبحانه وتعالى is saying that the Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) and Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), they submitted

828
01:04:50,240 --> 01:04:53,408
when they were in that position they were submitting to Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

829
01:04:55,130 --> 01:05:00,440
And that is Islam because Islam is submission to Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

830
01:05:01,281 --> 01:05:06,880
You fulfill the commandments of Allah, even if it's against your will,

831
01:05:07,063 --> 01:05:11,134
even if it's against your desires, even if it's against what you like.

832
01:05:12,698 --> 01:05:14,936
Nobody would want to slaughter his son.

833
01:05:15,698 --> 01:05:19,053
And no son would want his life to be taken away.

834
01:05:19,490 --> 01:05:25,355
But they're doing it as a form of worship Ibadah(عبادة) and that is Islam; submission.

835
01:05:26,252 --> 01:05:27,736
This is the meaning of Islam.

836
01:05:29,419 --> 01:05:31,411
فَلَمّا أَسلَما وَتَلَّهُ لِلجَبينِ۝

837
01:05:32,292 --> 01:05:40,055
When they were in that position, Ibrahim عليه السّلام had the knife on the neck of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل)

838
01:05:41,094 --> 01:05:44,484
and he started to pass the knife over is neck.

839
01:05:44,849 --> 01:05:47,031
And then Allah سبحانه وتعالى called Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

840
01:05:48,063 --> 01:05:49,706
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

841
01:05:49,865 --> 01:05:57,488
وَنادَيناهُ أَن يا إِبراهيمُ۝قَد صَدَّقتَ الرُّؤيا ۚ

842
01:05:57,518 --> 01:05:59,814
 You have fulfilled the dream.

843
01:06:01,377 --> 01:06:04,863
You have fulfilled it, the dream is fulfilled.

844
01:06:05,339 --> 01:06:06,926
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى told him;

845
01:06:06,956 --> 01:06:12,053
إِنَّ هٰذا لَهُوَ البَلاءُ المُبينُ۝

846
01:06:12,083 --> 01:06:15,417
Verily that indeed was a manifest trial.

847
01:06:16,202 --> 01:06:20,226
It was a test for you and you have passed the test.

848
01:06:21,306 --> 01:06:23,813
Does Allah سبحانه وتعالى need the blood of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل).

849
01:06:24,250 --> 01:06:28,535
Does need the flesh of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), does Allah need the life of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), Allah doesn't need it.

850
01:06:28,853 --> 01:06:30,126
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

851
01:06:30,206 --> 01:06:33,658
وَفَدَيناهُ بِذِبحٍ عَظيمٍ۝

852
01:06:33,688 --> 01:06:38,679
Verily that indeed was a manifest trial and we ransomed him with a great sacrifice.

853
01:06:40,512 --> 01:06:42,964
It was a test from Allah, Allah does not need the blood.

854
01:06:43,321 --> 01:06:48,794
Allah does not need the flesh, Allah does not need to take away the life of Ismael عليه السّلام

855
01:06:49,411 --> 01:06:52,538
this was a test and they both passed in the test.

856
01:06:52,799 --> 01:06:58,756
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى rewarded Ibrahim عليه السّلام with the sacrifice, A ram.

857
01:06:59,542 --> 01:07:05,357
Look at the results of Taqwa(تقوى) it was an action of Taqwa(تقوى) that Ibrahim عليه السّلام did.

858
01:07:05,873 --> 01:07:09,194
Allah سبحانه وتعالى rewarded him for it.

859
01:07:09,424 --> 01:07:17,842
And now we sacrifice in Eid Al-Ad'ha(عيدالأضحى) and Al-Hadie(ألهدي) in Al-Hajj(ألحَجْ), every year following the Sunnah(سنة) Syedina Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

860
01:07:19,009 --> 01:07:26,842
Ibrahim عليه السّلام was told by Allah سبحانه وتعالى or actually the Ayaat(آيات) say;

861
01:07:27,223 --> 01:07:33,944
وَتَرَكنا عَلَيهِ فِي الآخِرينَ۝ سَلامٌ عَلىٰ إِبراهيمَ۝

862
01:07:33,974 --> 01:07:39,433
And we left for him among generations in later times, Salam(سلام).

863
01:07:40,131 --> 01:07:47,251
After this event happened, Allah سبحانه وتعالى says and we left Salam(سلام) for Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) in the generations to come,

864
01:07:47,529 --> 01:07:51,624
and then and what is the representation of that?

865
01:07:52,052 --> 01:07:54,682
What is the representation of the Salam(سلام) Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم)?

866
01:07:57,039 --> 01:07:58,626
How is that manifested?

867
01:07:59,634 --> 01:08:02,191
It is in the Tsgahud(تشاهد), that we do in every Salah(صلاة).

868
01:08:03,358 --> 01:08:11,501
We make Salah(صلاة) and Salaam(سلام) on Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Muhammadﷺ in every Salah(صلاة).

869
01:08:12,478 --> 01:08:13,392
Allah سبحانه تعالى says;

870
01:08:13,422 --> 01:08:16,268
وَتَرَكنا عَلَيهِ فِي الآخِرينَ۝ سَلامٌ عَلىٰ إِبراهيمَ۝

871
01:08:16,501 --> 01:08:20,381
 And we left for him in the generations to come; Peace on Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

872
01:08:20,411 --> 01:08:23,498
We're asking Allah سبحانه وتعالى  to grant Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) peace and every Salah(صلاة).

873
01:08:23,712 --> 01:08:31,974
Millions and millions of believers all over the world, throughout generations, five times a day and more

874
01:08:32,190 --> 01:08:35,192
are asking Allah سبحانه وتعالى to grant Ibrahim عليه السّلام peace.

875
01:08:39,018 --> 01:08:41,605
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّم

